From dc3f6164acec7f496de10824163cd9cab44d33d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhouyllll <xuezhou28@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 09:14:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 39/49] arch/arm64/rk3576: move a functional assignment out of
 the DWMMC trace block

The SD card only worked when CONFIG_RK3576_DWMMC_TRACE was compiled in.
The reason is not timing: `priv->last_result = OK;` sat inside the
#ifdef, and it is the only place that ever sets last_result to success --
every failure path assigns outside it.  With tracing off, last_result
stayed at the -EBUSY written before each command, and recvshort/recvlong
open with `if (priv->last_result != OK) return priv->last_result;`, so
every response read failed.

"Works only with logging enabled" reads like a race that extra print
latency papers over, and that is where the search had been going --
delays, FIFO thresholds, clock setup.  It had nothing to do with
timing; conditional compilation had simply swallowed one assignment, and
nothing in the build warns about it.

Rule that follows: an #ifdef'd debug block may print and count, nothing
else.  Toggling a debug option must not change behaviour.

With this, /dev/mmcsd1 enumerates with tracing off.

