From 8452ea2fa22740508eafb828f2f5425af20de084 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhouyllll <xuezhou28@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 04:49:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 45/49] arch/arm64/rk3576: bring up SMP on the four Cortex-A53
 cores

RK3576 is 4x Cortex-A53 (MPIDR 0x0-0x3, Aff1=0) + 4x Cortex-A72
(0x100-0x103, Aff1=1), all with enable-method "psci" and a psci node
of method "smc" (rk3576.dtsi).  Add the chip-level CPU index <-> MPIDR
mapping the generic layer requires, and declare the two capabilities
the SMP path depends on:

  - ARCH_HAVE_MULTICPU   arm64_get_mpid()/arm64_get_cpuid()
  - ARCH_HAVE_IRQTRIGGER up_trigger_irq(), used by arm64_smpcall.c to
                         raise SGI9/SGI11 through the GICv2

Only the A53 cluster is used for now, so the generic Aff0-based
CORE_TO_MPID/MPID_TO_CORE are correct as-is.  Extending to eight cores
needs a custom mapping that also folds in Aff1, since the A72 cluster
would otherwise alias onto 0..3.  The A72 cluster is also the half
earmarked for Linux in the AMP work, so leaving it out now costs
nothing.

While here, declare ARCH_HAVE_SDIO from RK3576_DWMMC: the driver
provides an SDIO lower half but never advertised it, so MMCSD_SDIO
could not be selected from a clean defconfig.

Measured on KICKPI-K7: ps shows idle tasks Running on CPU0..CPU3 with
affinity 0xf; cmocka_sched_test 16/16 (scheduled onto CPU1); ostest
exits 0 with smp_call_test reporting success on all four variants.

