From 3b51eaa18ba0ef362ad5404f46795386314fccd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhouyllll <xuezhou28@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 17:13:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 49/49] arch/arm64: move the RK3576 chip layer out of the core
 repo
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The openvela porting guide is explicit: 所有定制代码存放在 vendor 目录中,
不得修改核心代码 -- all custom code lives under vendor/, the core repo is
not to be modified.  The chip layer sat in arch/arm64/src/rk3576/ with a
matching ARCH_CHIP_RK3576 entry in arch/arm64/Kconfig, which is exactly
the modification the guide rules out.  It also collided with the contest
rule that discounts work done in the NuttX kernel repo.

NuttX already supports out-of-tree chips and arm64 already exposes the
option, so no core change is needed to enable this:

  ARCH_CHIP_ARM64_CUSTOM -> ARCH_CHIP_CUSTOM
  ARCH_CHIP_CUSTOM_DIR / _DIR_RELPATH / _NAME

tools/Config.mk derives CHIP_DIR and CHIP_KCONFIG from those, and
tools/Unix.mk links arch/arm64/src/chip and include/arch/chip at them and
copies the chip's Kconfig over arch/dummy/Kconfig.  The 64 chip files now
live in the team repo at chip/rk3576/ and are picked up from there.

Two details worth recording, because neither is obvious from the docs:

  * The selects that used to hang off the ARCH_CHIP_RK3576 entry have no
    home once that entry is gone.  They move into the chip's own Kconfig
    on a hidden  that defaults to y.

  * CONFIG_ARCH_CHIP_CUSTOM has to appear in the defconfig verbatim, not
    merely be selected by ARCH_CHIP_ARM64_CUSTOM.  Config.mk is read by
    make before kconfig has resolved any select, so a selected-only symbol
    leaves CHIP_KCONFIG pointing at the empty arch/dummy/dummy_kconfig --
    the chip's whole Kconfig is then silently absent and every
    CONFIG_RK3576_* option is dropped from .config.

What stays in the core repo is what the driver guide says belongs there:
drivers/timers/hym8563.c (a new shareable I2C RTC driver) and a one-line
fix to drivers/input/ft5x06.c.  Both are generic, neither is board
specific, and both should go upstream as their own PRs rather than ride
along with the board port.

Verified: libarch.a carries 25 rk3576 objects and the linked image 139
rk3576 symbols, all compiled from the out-of-tree location.

